 This install applies to "Hard Drivin'" (c) 1989/1990 Tengen/Atari/Domark.
 Version 4.0b (04.11.2026)

 Requirements:
 -------------
 An original copy of the game and WHDLoad version 17.0 or later are required.
 WHDLoad must be accessible in the command path.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem.
 Additional memory is needed to preload the game files. PRELOAD is recommended
 to avoid repeated disk access. An A1200 with Fast RAM is recommended for
 enhanced gameplay.

 The game requires an A500 Kickstart 1.3 image named "kick34005.A500" in
 "Devs:Kickstarts", together with "kick34005.A500.RTB". The image can be
 extracted from an A500 with GrabKick or a similar tool from Aminet.
 An incorrect or altered image will be rejected by WHDLoad. The RTB file
 is available in "util/boot/skick346.lha" on Aminet.

 Supported editions:
 - Original release
 - TNT compilation (same disk as Toobin')
 - Wheels Of Fire compilation (same disk as Chase HQ)
 - ReSpray budget release
 - Racing Masters compilation

 The new enhancements have been tested with the original SPS 0126 edition.
 The other supported editions retain their existing patches. Action 5,
 Summer Smashers and Sport Games Hits editions remain unverified.

 Installation:
 -------------
 Extract the package, double-click "Install" and follow the prompts.
 Select the game edition, destination drawer and preferred icon. Existing
 support for floppy disks and disk images is retained. Installing from disk
 images requires the additional tools described by the installer's help.
 For Wheels Of Fire, select the file named "2" (49804 bytes) when requested.
 The installer creates a HardDrivin drawer with the game files in "data".

 Features:
 ---------
 Start the game from its icon. Steering and menus use the mouse; see Arcade
 controls below for the buttons with arcade handling.
 High scores are loaded from and saved to hard disk.

 Keys:
   Q       Abort the current race.
   Esc/F10 Quit to Workbench. F10 is the default WHDLoad QuitKey, which can
           be changed with the QuitKey tooltype.

 CUSTOM2 controls the existing frame delay: 0 gives maximum rendering speed;
 higher values slow rendering down.

 The options below affect only the original SPS 0126 edition. Set them in
 the WHDLoad splash window or as tooltypes.

 Simulation (CUSTOM1):
   Original (0)
       The original simulation and renderer.
   Enhanced framerate (1)
       Smoother gameplay on accelerated Amigas with the original Amiga
       handling, including its abrupt skids.
   Enhanced framerate with arcade handling (2)
       As Enhanced framerate, with the car driving like the arcade
       machine's. This is the default for newly installed icons.
 Command-line launches must specify CUSTOM1=1 or CUSTOM1=2 to enable the
 enhanced simulations.

 Enhanced framerate:
 Movement, physics, traffic and replay timing use elapsed time. On 68020 and
 faster CPUs, physics can update every PAL field (50 times per second); the
 renderer draws as often as it can. On 68000, physics updates follow rendered
 frames. Original race-clock behaviour and its defects are retained unless
 arcade race timing is selected.

 Both enhanced settings also draw the road and the objects on it in depth
 order, so cars no longer appear in front of scenery that hides them, and
 let traffic slow down behind a slower car in its lane instead of driving
 through it.

 Rendering optimizations are selected automatically: optimized rotations and
 blitter waits on 68000, and on 68020 with the executable in Fast RAM; optimized
 rotations on 68040/68060, and the original renderer on 68030. Other untested
 configurations retain the original renderer. CUSTOM3 is not a release option.

 Arcade handling:
 The car follows the arcade machine's own car model: tyre grip and slides,
 weight transfer, springs, the engine and automatic gearbox, and the brakes.
 The course is driven at its real scale, so speeds match the scenery. Ramps,
 jumps and the loop follow the arcade, including falling off the loop when
 too slow. Crashes follow the arcade's rules: a wall is only a crash when hit
 hard, objects are a crash above about 40 MPH, and landings never are.

 Arcade controls (mouse):
   Mouse left/right  Steer. Steering is gentle around the centre and quicker
                     towards full lock, for fine corrections at speed.
   Right button      Gas pedal. Hold it to open the throttle (fully in about
                     0.2 seconds); release it and the throttle closes over
                     0.4 seconds.
   Left button       Brake pedal. A single press brakes at about a third of
                     the pedal, which slows the car while it still turns.
                     Press again within half a second and hold (a double
                     click) for full braking: the front wheels lock, and the
                     car stops hardest but hardly steers. Release to let go.
 Lifting off or braking in a fast corner moves weight off the rear wheels
 and can start a slide, as in the arcade; steer into the slide to catch it.
 The gears are automatic or manual as selected in the game. These pedals
 apply to mouse control; other control methods keep the game's own throttle.

 Arcade brake (CUSTOM4), with arcade handling:
   Full (0)  The arcade's brake, locking the front wheels at full pedal.
   Soft (1)  A weaker brake that stops short of locking the front wheels
             and comes on more gradually.

 Race timing (CUSTOM5), with any Simulation setting:
   Amiga (0)   The game's own clocks.
   Arcade (1)  The arcade's race timing: the countdown runs in real time,
               checkpoint time limits follow the arcade (doubled unless arcade
               handling is selected, as the other settings cross the course
               at half speed), the difficulty in the options menu selects the
               arcade's matching difficulty, and the championship lap needs
               the arcade's qualifying time, shown on the dashboard from the
               start.

 This is a beta with limited human playtesting. Enhancements can add
 overhead on an A500, and arcade handling adds more; they are not a promise
 of higher frame rates on every setup.

 History:
 --------
 version 4.0b (04.11.2026) done by Vesa Halttunen:
 - added a Simulation option for the SPS 0126 edition: Original, Enhanced
   framerate, or Enhanced framerate with arcade handling, the default for
   new installs
 - Enhanced framerate: smoother gameplay on faster Amigas with the original
   handling; traffic, replays and related animation and sound timing follow
   elapsed time; automatic CPU-specific rendering optimizations
 - arcade handling: the arcade machine's car model, driven at the course's
   real scale, with the mouse buttons as gas and brake pedals, a steering
   response suited to the mouse, and the arcade's ramps, jumps, loop and
   crash rules
 - added an Arcade brake option, Full or Soft, for arcade handling
 - added a Race timing option, Amiga or Arcade
 - with the enhanced settings, the road and objects are drawn in depth order
   so cars no longer show through scenery, and traffic follows a slower car
   in its lane instead of driving through it
 - fixed rare renderer crashes present in the original game
 - updated the installer using the WHDLoad Install Template, retaining all
   five game editions and seven icon choices

 version 3.0 (23.03.2024) done by JOTD:
 - fixed keyboard on version SPS0126 (issue #0006342)
 - source code reworked & available
 
 version 2.04 (06/2008) done by Girv:
 - fixed crash bug when saving high scores (introduced with 2.03)

 v 2.03    03/2008
      - supports Racing Masters compilation version
      - upgraded installer script to latest version
      - added some new icons
      - requires WHDLoad v16.5+
 v 2.02    01/2005
      - supports ReSpray budget version
 v 2.01    01/2005
      - supports TNT compilation version
      - supports Wheels Of Fire compilation version
 v 2.00    12/2004
      - rewritten to use Kickstart emulation
      - fixed blthog usage
      - fixed access errors
      - fixed more cpu dependent delay loops
      - fixed self modifying graphics code
      - WHDLoad v16.0 compatible
      - uses standard release numbering system
      - uses standard WHDLoad installer script
 v 0801.1  08/2001
      - uses OSEmu 20010818
      - version checks moved from installer script into slave
      - miscellaneous installer script improvements
      - fixed cpu dependent delay loops

 v 0601.1  06/2001
      - fixed file loading crash bug
 
 v 0501.1  05/2001
      - first release
      - fixed to run with fastram and caches
      - fixed gear selection bug
      - fixed access violation
      - added high score loading/saving
      - added framerate control
      - added "abort game" key

